.TH "CIRCLECI-MIGRATE" "1" "Jun 2026" "circleci-migrate" "CircleCI Org Migration CLI"

.SH NAME
circleci-migrate-mapping - Generate and manage project slug mapping files.


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcircleci-migrate mapping [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
mapping provides utilities for creating the mapping.json file that tells
\&'sync' and 'secrets transfer' how source project slugs correspond to
destination project slugs.

.PP
The most common use is 'mapping generate', which auto-matches projects by
repo name (the last segment of the slug) so you don't have to hand-write
mapping.json for a standard org rename.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for mapping


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	Enable debug logging

.PP
\fB--dest-token\fP=""
	API token for the destination org (env: CIRCLECI_DEST_TOKEN)

.PP
\fB--host\fP="https://circleci.com"
	CircleCI host URL (env: CIRCLECI_CLI_HOST, CIRCLECI_HOST, or CIRCLE_URL)

.PP
\fB--source-token\fP=""
	API token for the source org (env: CIRCLECI_SOURCE_TOKEN)

.PP
\fB--token\fP=""
	Personal API token — fallback for both orgs (env: CIRCLECI_CLI_TOKEN or CIRCLE_TOKEN)


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBcircleci-migrate(1)\fP, \fBcircleci-migrate-mapping-generate(1)\fP
